      "body": "## Motivation\n\nA periodic HF3FS metadata save copies the key-to-page mapping under the rank lock but retains a reference to the mutable free-page list. If an HTTP deletion releases a page before JSON serialization, the file can mark that page both free and assigned. After restart, allocating another key can give both keys the same page. A concurrent reservation can instead remove capacity from the saved snapshot without recording its new owner.\n\n## Modifications\n\nCopy the free-page list while holding the existing rank lock. Each saved rank then contains a consistent free-list/mapping snapshot without holding locks during file I/O. The persistence format and ordinary allocation behavior stay unchanged.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- Two deterministic regressions fail before the fix: an actual HTTP deletion during persistence creates conflicting page ownership after reload, and a concurrent reservation removes a free page from the captured snapshot. Both gate the real JSON serializer and join the saving thread before checking results.\n- A roundtrip control preserves free pages, key order, and separate rank/pool namespaces.\n- All 3 tests and all matching pre-commit hooks pass. The actual HTTP/delete/save/reload/allocation reproduction now restores distinct pages for the old and new keys.\n\nCPU validation uses actual metadata classes, FastAPI TestClient, JSON files, reload, and allocation. The local harness excludes GPU/backend import initialization; no GPU or native HF3FS I/O is claimed. This change ensures internal metadata-snapshot consistency, not atomic persistence with ongoing storage-file writes.\n\nPrepared and independently reviewed with AI assistance (Codex).\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo throughput claim. The change copies the free-page list once per metadata save while the existing rank lock is held.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format code according to the contribution guide.\n- [x] Add regression tests.\n- [x] Documentation: no public API or persistence-format change.\n- [x] Provide applicable validation above; GPU accuracy/speed benchmarks are not applicable.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\n\n## Combined review validation, October 13\n\nApplied #42059, #42081 and #42082 together to main `684fea8af3b11a5b51ec9966c02959a32ad3421c` in an isolated checkout. All three patches apply cleanly. The combined capacity, snapshot and shutdown suites pass: 13 test methods and 3 subtests. Running the same tests against main without the fixes reproduces the capacity, snapshot and shutdown failures.\n\nThis CPU harness executes the repository metadata classes and tests with real FastAPI, threading and JSON persistence, while excluding unrelated GPU and native backend import initialization. This is combined source validation, not native HF3FS or GPU coverage. The latest base CI gate stops before these tests because the required `run-ci` label is missing.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #36881241776](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36881241776)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #36881241038](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36881241038)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #36881241175](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36881241175)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
